# ALL.mask -- line masks for rosetta-unicon (FORMAT: entry<TAB>python-regex<TAB>reason), read by corpus_suite_harness.py read_mask_sidecar().
average-loop-length	PART:^ *[0-9]+ +([0-9.]+) +[0-9.]+ +(-?[0-9.]+)%$	the measured average and its percentage difference come from a million random draws a row (?n-1): two oracle runs print 1.4997 and another 1.5003 for n=2, a machine value masked in both streams alike; n, the expected column and the rest of each line stay graded, 13 of 29 characters at most (suites-and-grading section 4, the part mask; row unicon-every-no-oracle-answer-exclusion-is-measured-again-and-cut-or-says-why)
